&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CIVIL PROJECT MANAGER, STARBASE DEVELOPMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Starbase Development team, you will lead the delivery of civil construction projects across residential, commercial, and industrial settings that ultimately support the rapid production of Starship.&amp;nbsp;You will manage projects from conception through construction completion and closeout, coordinating with stakeholders, engineers, and construction teams across multiple disciplines to build out the Starbase campus as the gateway to Mars.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage civil infrastructure projects end-to-end, including design, permitting, procurement, construction, and close-out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project scope, schedule, and budget from conception through closeout for residential subdivisions, commercial amenities and community recreational projects; actively drive projects to meet target budgets and timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact between design teams, utility operational teams, facilities maintenance groups, stakeholders, contractors, subcontractors, and local municipal or utility authorities having jurisdiction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage permitting and inspection processes with internal utility operational teams, and local jurisdictions and authorities having jurisdiction (AHJs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write, negotiate, and manage design and construction contracts with subcontractors across multiple disciplines through contract close-out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve design and construction conflicts in the field in real time, prioritizing pragmatic, fast-moving solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support with long-term utility and civil planning for future phases of development and master planning for Starbase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on new projects ad-hoc as the business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in architecture, construction management, or engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing civil construction projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing residential land development or community master planning infrastructure projects (utilities, land platting and subdivision, roadways, amenities)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with grading plans and cut/fill analyses, stormwater design and management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of power and network distribution systems, water distribution and wastewater collection systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with landscaping design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with AutoCAD software, Civil 3D, Bluebeam Revu and project scheduling software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication and negotiation skills, and ability to represent SpaceX to external municipal and utility teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and works autonomously and efficiently in a dynamic team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Licensed Professional Engineer (PE) in the state of Texas or Project Management Professional (PMP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is based in Starbase, TX and requires being onsite – remote work not considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel to various SpaceX locations for mission critical projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible to work extended hours and/or weekends to align with residential project deadlines and site operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
