&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CONSTRUCTION SUPERINTENDENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Texas Construction Projects team, you will be responsible for overseeing the coordination and field execution of facilities construction projects. You will work with design engineers, construction project managers, facilities and maintenance technicians, vendors, and internal partners to support these goals. You will have the opportunity to drive positive change and own projects from start to finish, with the goal of making SpaceX projects into world-class facilities. This position is based in McGregor, TX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate facilities projects to ensure vendors meet standards while delivering promised services, materials, and craftsmanship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and direct construction activities of internal resources as well as all involved subcontractors for each phase of construction and lead any coordination meetings between trades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hand-in-hand with the Texas Construction Projects team to maintain accurate records of daily logs, progress reports, and financial reports related to the construction of facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce contract expectations from subcontractors and communicate any discrepancies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approve work being performed by subcontractors and handle any related issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authorize payments to subcontractors upon thorough inspection of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a safe work site by implementing safety requirements, enforcing safe work habits, and observing OSHA requirements and any applicable agency regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify all checklists are complete and inspections are scheduled and passed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor cleanliness and hold subcontractors responsible for daily clean-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule and manage subcontractors to make designated warranty repairs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain rapport with subcontractors, operators, and inspectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate inspections with local officials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and manage project request tickets, including creating work orders when needed and managing their completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create purchase orders as necessary to support timely project execution, including but not limited to rentals, materials, or subcontractor labor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in the construction industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience leading the coordination of multiple trades on-site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of electrical, plumbing, heating, ventilation, air conditioning and refrigeration (HVAC/R), concrete, framing, and industrial gas trades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of basic engineering and construction principles and methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conduct all business in a professional and ethical manner to serve customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in reading and interpreting engineering drawings, specifications, and calculations; ability to mark up and highlight coordination items&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently and effectively manage projects in an extremely fast-paced and changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite tools and PDF editor software such as Bluebeam or Adobe Acrobat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a high-stress environment balancing several projects at any given time and the flexibility to adjust for abrupt changes in strategic direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
