&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ELECTRICIAN, SOLAR CELLS (STARLINK) - DAY SHIFT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SpaceX, we are building the next generation of space infrastructure to enable large-scale AI data centers in orbit. These orbital AI platforms require massive amounts of reliable, high-efficiency solar power to support intensive computing workloads in space. To make this possible, we are standing up one of the largest solar cell manufacturing facilities in the world. We are seeking an Electrician to install, maintain, and repair electrical distribution, controls, and power systems for both facility infrastructure and solar cell production equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, maintain, and repair electrical distribution, controls, lighting, and power systems for facility infrastructure and production equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support power systems for cleanroom tools, utility equipment, and process areas including PECVD, PVD, texturing, and metallization lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform preventive and corrective maintenance on electrical systems to ensure reliability and minimal downtime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot electrical issues down to the component level using schematics and diagnostic tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with facilities and production teams to develop and follow work instructions and safety procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with National Electrical Code (NEC), OSHA, and all applicable safety standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in continuous improvement initiatives for electrical system performance and energy efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open and resolve electronic work tickets and maintain accurate documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience as a licensed or certified electrician in an industrial or manufacturing setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Journeyman or master electrician license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with industrial electrical systems, controls, and power distribution in cleanroom or high-tech manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting skills and ability to read and interpret electrical schematics, P&amp;amp;IDs, and blueprints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting high-volume production equipment and utility systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cleanroom protocols and gowning procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with lock-out/tag-out, job hazard analysis, and chemical safety protocols&lt;/li&gt;
