&lt;p&gt;This role will work for the Cape Canaveral Lead Environmental Engineer to run the site’s environmental programs at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station (CCSFS) and Kennedy Space Center (KSC). The engineer will work in a cross-functional environment to maintain monitoring, permitting, and reporting programs, and will provide technical expertise on design reviews and operational plans. The ideal candidate is highly skilled in environmental compliance and works well in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve environmental programs for SpaceX operations at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station and Kennedy Space Center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain compliance with applicable federal, Florida, and installation requirements, including EPA (Region 4), RCRA, EPCRA, CWA/NPDES, CAA, SPCC, Florida Department of Environmental Protection (FDEP), St. Johns River Water Management District (SJRWMD) as applicable, NASA KSC, and Space Launch Delta 45 / CCSFS environmental policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use continuous chemical inventory outputs to prepare, quality-check, and submit EPCRA Tier II and TRI filings on schedule; archive calculations and submission packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain hazardous materials inventories and business-plan / emergency-planning inputs for installation, county, and state reporting (including Florida SERC/LEPC and host-installation hazardous materials requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain air permit recordkeeping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and manage contractors for permitting and environmental testing. Review and maintain reports and other relevant records from assessments and permitting activities (air, wastewater, stormwater, waste, and storage tanks as assigned)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in planning for changes in physical facilities, reviewing new or modified equipment, and new programs to meet regulatory and permitting requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain positive relationships with federal, state, county, NASA KSC, and Space Launch Delta 45 / CCSFS regulators and environmental counterparts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain positive, close working relationships with engineering, facilities, launch, and processing teams across the Cape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with process owners on equipment/process buy-off and high-hazard chemical operations as they affect air, waste, water, or hazardous materials programs; coordinate source tests, stack testing, and field work with consultants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform internal audits and inspections of environmental programs and recordkeeping; drive corrective actions with operations, facilities, and launch stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience operating or building environmental compliance programs in an industrial, aerospace, DoD, or manufacturing setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in environmental engineering, environmental science/management, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in Florida (or comparable authorized-state) environmental compliance, preferably at an aerospace, launch, NASA, or federal facility, owning environmental programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of FDEP air permitting (construction/operating, Title V where applicable), EPCRA Tier II/TRI, RCRA hazardous waste, SPCC, NPDES/MSGP stormwater, and installation-host environmental processes at KSC and/or CCSFS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience utilizing AI for process optimization and automation of recordkeeping tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills. Experience handling highly technical data and technical data interpretation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of successful analysis, interpretation, and application of rules and regulations toward practical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work well in an integrated collaborative team environment, including frequent interactions with other engineers, managers, and federal, state, county, NASA, and USSF agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle many projects at once, prioritize work, and work efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly self-motivated and able to prioritize and execute tasks in a high-pressure environment with ongoing drive for continuous improvement in all aspects of work&lt;/li&gt;
