&lt;p&gt;As a member of the HQ construction team, you will design, build, and activate some of the world’s most technically advanced manufacturing facilities. As a member of the critical construction and facilities infrastructure team, you will design, build and maintain fire protection and life safety systems. You will be the subject matter expert in the following areas: fire protection, life safety, building and fire codes, fire hazard and risk assessment of materials and processes, fire and smoke spread, industrial fire hazards, fire investigation support, and other fire and life safety issues. You will be able to operate with autonomy to solve diverse and complex problems, excel at managing multiple projects at a time and work in a dynamic, fast-paced environment. You will work with other construction engineers, architects and internal customers to support these goals and have the opportunity to drive real global impact, ultimately leading to making life multiplanetary. The position is based in Hawthorne, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support engineering design, analysis, calculations and specifications for facility infrastructure fire and life safety systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop building and fire code compliance documents and fire life safety designs for SpaceX launch and production facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform hazardous material analysis for code compliances purposes, such as chemical classification, chemical quantity analysis, chemical inventory management, and related system design support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support facility construction teams to develop field solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support commissioning activities during pre-test and AHJ testing phases for launch site facility builds&lt;/li&gt;
