&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLUID SYSTEMS ENGINEER, STARLINK INFRASTRUCTURE&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Starlink Infrastructure team is building world-class production facilities in Bastrop, Texas to support vertically integrated manufacturing of solar cells, user terminals, and PCBAs, along with terrestrial and in-space SI data centers. The specialty fluid systems behind these factories are the backbone of production, and this team owns them end to end: chemical and specialty gas delivery, cryogenic storage and distribution, zero-liquid discharge wastewater processing, Air-separation units, and freshwater intake and treatment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Fluid Systems Engineer, you will lead the design, build, and commissioning of these systems. You will be the extreme owner for your systems, carrying novel designs from first requirement through activation and sustained operation. The problems are real and the scale is large: high-volume chip fabrication, solar production, SI compute, and a rapidly expanding constellation of Starlink satellites all depend on the infrastructure this team delivers. This is the future of American manufacturing, built from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and activate fluids systems for distribution of bulk and specialty gases, chemicals (e.g., hydrofluoric acid, solvents), exhaust systems, and zero-liquid discharge wastewater plants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects cradle to grave: requirement definition, design, justification of key decisions, equipment procurement, build coordination, commissioning, and project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as project manager for facility construction, developing and maintaining schedules, cost estimates, and budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage in-field construction and contractor relationships as the primary point of contact for contracted work, with responsibility for safety, schedule, and field coordination; eliminate blockers and drive the critical path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage selection, procurement, installation, and activation of bulk storage tanks, pumps, heat exchangers, gas panels, valves, scrubbers, and abatement systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply fluids and mechanical engineering fundamentals, including P&amp;amp;ID development, equipment sizing, detailed fluid and thermal analysis, system-level CONOP development, structural analysis, and materials and component selection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform safety and hazard assessments (e.g., FMEAs, HAZOPs) for hazardous system design, including emergency shutdown CONOPs, redundancy, and compliance with hazardous material safety standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory compliance with OSHA, EPA, ASME, NFPA, and SEMI standards for chemical and gas handling, and collaborate with fire and life safety engineers to meet code requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and deploy data acquisition and control systems for fluids facility control and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with process engineers to integrate fluids systems with manufacturing equipment and optimize delivery rates, purity levels, and recovery and recycling of process fluids for high-yield production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support installation, commissioning, and troubleshooting alongside facilities operations, EHS, automation, and procurement teams to resolve issues and implement improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track system performance metrics (e.g., flow rates, contamination levels, downtime) and drive continuous improvement, including lean manufacturing and fluid reuse initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
