&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position requires successfully obtaining and maintaining a Top Secret Security Clearance as a condition of employment. While the clearance may not be immediately necessary upon hire, we encourage you to initiate the application process promptly upon accepting this offer. Your ability to secure the necessary clearance is essential for fulfilling key responsibilities of the role. Should you be unable to obtain it, SpaceX reserves the right to modify or terminate your employment to align with operational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work extended hours and weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pay Range:&lt;br&gt;Level 1: $125,000.00 - $150,000.00&lt;br&gt;Level 2: $145,000.00 - $175,000.00&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of your total rewards package at SpaceX. You may also be eligible for long-term incentives, in the form of company stock or long-term cash awards, as well as potential discretionary bonuses and the ability to purchase additional stock at a discount through an Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You will also receive access to comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, paid parental leave, and various other discounts and perks. You may also accrue 3 weeks of paid vacation and will be eligible for 10 or more paid holidays per year. Employees accrue paid sick leave pursuant to Company policy which satisfies or exceeds the accrual, carryover, and use requirements of the law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GAS &amp;amp; CHEMICAL TECHNICIAN, SOLAR CELLS (STARLINK) - DAY SHIFT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SpaceX, we are building the next generation of space infrastructure to enable large-scale AI data centers in orbit. These orbital AI platforms require massive amounts of reliable, high-efficiency solar power to support intensive computing workloads in space. To make this possible, we are standing up one of the largest solar cell manufacturing facilities in the world. We are seeking a Gas &amp;amp; Chemical Technician to manage the safe receipt, distribution, monitoring, and recovery of process gases and wet chemicals used in high-volume solar cell production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the safe receipt, distribution, monitoring, storage, and recovery of process gases (including phosphine, silane, ammonia, hydrogen, NF3, diborane, and others) and wet chemicals used in texturing, diffusion, PECVD, etching, and cleaning steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform startup, shutdown, and monitoring of gas cabinets, chemical delivery systems, and abatement equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process deviations, perform corrective actions, and maintain process parameters through chemical analysis, additions, and system adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot, maintain, and calibrate gas and chemical handling equipment while ensuring design integrity and product quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineering teams to develop operating procedures, provide design feedback, and support root cause analysis for issues impacting yield or uptime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safely handle, transport, and load hazardous chemicals and gases while adhering to all safety protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect, segregate, and manage chemical waste streams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and perform preventive maintenance and calibration of gas and chemical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain inventory of consumables and critical spares&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure 5S standards and a clean, organized work area while upholding all safety, quality, and environmental policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience working in a hands-on technical position in a chemical handling environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling flammable, toxic, corrosive, or hazardous gases and chemicals (including silane, phosphine, and acids)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of gas delivery systems, chemical distribution, abatement/scrubbers, and safety interlocks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in semiconductor, solar, or high-volume manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting skills and ability to read and understand P&amp;amp;IDs, schematics, and technical documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cleanroom protocols and gowning procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with lock-out/tag-out, job hazard analysis, and chemical safety protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Office tools and executing digital work instructions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated punctuality, ability to work in a high-stress environment, and flexibility to adjust priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand up to 6 hours, lift up to 25 pounds unassisted, and maneuver around equipment in a factory setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in industrial environments with fumes/odors, noise, hazardous chemicals, and confined spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available for one of the following AWS shifts (start and end times are approximate):
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Shift – 5:00am-5:00pm, Sunday-Wednesday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B Shift – 5:00am-5:00pm, Wednesday-Saturday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GATEWAY FLEET SPECIALIST:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Starlink is building the world’s largest fleet of satellite ground stations. These gateways are the critical link between our satellites and the global internet backbone, and their reliability directly determines the quality of service for millions of users.&amp;nbsp;We are seeking fleet specialists to own the reliability, growth, and sustainment of our fleet of Gateway antennas and sites across a region of the world. This is a true owner-operator role, managing everything from technical troubleshooting and spare parts strategy to international logistics, contractor performance, and field execution.&amp;nbsp;This role is ideal for someone who excels at building operational excellence in fast-moving and internationally complex environments. You must be equally comfortable managing heavy equipment deployments in remote locations as you are negotiating with customs authorities and&amp;nbsp;coaching contractors toward higher performance standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the maintenance, operations, health, and growth for our fleet of Starlink Gateway Antennas and Sites for a region of the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage spare parts strategy, inventory planning, and materials movement across the region,&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;maintain rapid response readiness for both planned and emergency maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor fleet health using dashboards and telemetry data to identify issues, diagnose software and hardware failures, drive timely repairs, and identify emerging degradation trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering teams to execute fleetwide campaigns and perform root cause analysis&amp;nbsp;on antenna and site failures across electrical, fiber optic, radiofrequency, and mechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with logistics providers, customs authorities, and regional partners to ensure timely and compliant international shipping of critical parts and equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with contracted labor in the region, including training and capability development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze operational data and field feedback to identify systemic pain points and drive improvements in processes and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share ownership of the team’s growth: work with engineers and specialists to build scalable organizational structures that can support the rapid expansion of the world’s largest fleet of satellite ground stations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience operations, logistics, technical support, field service, data analytics, project management, or a similar role involving distributed assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in a customer support associate, technical support associate, quality specialist, process planner, business analyst, or leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with satellite ground stations,&amp;nbsp;antennas; electrical, fiber optic, radiofrequency, or mechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting geographically distributed technical equipment or infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience querying and analyzing data using SQL and/or other data visualization tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in root cause analysis and cross-functional collaboration with engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing contractors or third-party vendors, particularly in international or remote environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with MRP/ERP systems and spare parts/inventory management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in one or more of the following languages&amp;nbsp;(in addition to English): Portuguese, French,&amp;nbsp;Punjabi,&amp;nbsp;Hindi, Japanese, Bengali, Kazakh, Arabic, Urdu, Vietnamese, Swahili, Sesotho, Swati, Tagalog.&amp;nbsp;Knowledge of local business culture is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting or working with IT/network infrastructure (UPS, PDUs, servers, or networking equipment)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to design efficient processes and systems, especially defining requirements for software tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience autonomously managing projects with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel 10-15% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work extended hours and weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work outside of normal business hours 20-40% if the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pay Range:&lt;br&gt;Level 1: $27.00 - $40.00&lt;br&gt;Level 2: $31.00 - $45.00&lt;br&gt;Level 3: $36.00 - $51.00&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of your total rewards package at SpaceX. You may also be eligible for long-term incentives, in the form of company stock or long-term cash awards, as well as potential discretionary bonuses and the ability to purchase additional stock at a discount through an Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You will also receive access to comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, paid parental leave, and various other discounts and perks. You may also accrue 3 weeks of paid vacation and will be eligible for 10 or more paid holidays per year. Employees in Washington State accrue paid sick time in compliance with state and federal law. Company shuttles are offered to employees for roundtrip travel from select Seattle locations to the SpaceX Redmond office Monday to Friday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
