&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop highly reliable and performant GNC algorithms, simulations, tools, services, and dashboards using C++ or Python; Starfall GNC Engineers write actual production code, not just prototypes for transcription by another team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in architecture, design, and code reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bulk data analysis to review performance data from Starfall flights, simulations, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write high quality technical documentation of programs, algorithms, or analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entry vehicle trajectory design, guidance, and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Atmospheric entry, descent, and landing (EDL) algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Precision navigation and state estimation for reentry and recovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attitude determination and control during orbital, deorbit, and atmospheric flight phases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fleet-level or multi-vehicle coordination for logistics delivery and recovery operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simulation, analysis, and performance evaluation of entry systems under a wide range of conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integration of GNC with vehicle systems supporting military logistics and in-space manufacturing missions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, aerospace, physics or an engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of software development experience in either C++ or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree or PhD in an engineering discipline or physics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developed, debugged and deployed software that has been used in real world applications/projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative approach to problem solving, exceptional analytical skills and engineering fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with atmospheric entry guidance, navigation, and control for capsules or reentry vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of orbital mechanics, deorbit planning, and entry trajectory optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in verifying GNC algorithm performance via simulation, and validation of the simulation&#39;s models (including atmospheric, aerodynamic, and thermal environments)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with state estimation, particularly for reentry vehicles (IMU, GNSS, radar/optical, or other sensors)&lt;/li&gt;
