&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LEAD DEVELOPMENT TEST ENGINEER (STARLINK)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is looking for a Lead Development Test Engineer to oversee a team responsible for development and qualification test of satellite hardware in Bastrop. This individual owns design, activation, safety, and reliability of thermal, fluids, chamber, structural, and vibration test capability (HASS, HALT, TVAC, static/dynamic/vibe). The role spans design, analysis, and manufacturing. You will take large-scope projects from early trades through implementation, define processes, drive requirements, and activate systems that meet the bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of engineers enabling rapid hardware development through test — thermal, fluids, environmental chambers, structural, vibration, and dynamic test&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and own development-focused thermal chambers (HASS / HALT) and, as capability stands up, TVAC — hardware, fixturing, profiles, instrumentation, controls/dashboards, safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee structural, vibration, pressure, and related mechanical test: test article and stand configuration, boundary conditions, schematics, CONOPS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as technical decision maker and advisor to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop direct reports; set clear goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, document, and implement cross-functional testing solutions (capability, coverage, safety)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement GSE: fixtures, automated test equipment, facilities infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and activate stands with engineers and technicians; partner with Development Operations for fab (you do not own technician people ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in mechanical engineering or other engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands-on design, analysis, build, and test&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ year leading a product development, manufacturing engineering, or project team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with CAD, FEA, and/or FEM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional test experience (development test, environmental test, qual, or I&amp;amp;T)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with thermal HASS and/or HALT chambers (ran, specified, or owned campaigns)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with structural and/or vibration testing (static, dynamic, vibe, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TVAC / thermal-vacuum campaigns (owned or operated)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both thermal-chamber and structural/vibe campaigns (not only one)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and activation of fluids, thermal, vacuum, structural, or electromechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-cycle ownership of a hardware or test campaign from concept through implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hazardous systems (high pressure, high energy, fluids)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chamber automation, profiles, fixturing, DAQ (strain, PT, load, TC), NCR closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation / scripting (Python, C++, SQL, PLC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NX, SolidWorks, EPLAN&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong desire to mentor and develop engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work weekends and extended hours as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LEAD DEVELOPMENT TEST TECHNICIAN (STARSHIP STRUCTURAL TEST) – 1ST SHIFT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help lead a small team in support of testing operations, handing out work assignments based on priorities, enforcing safety &amp;amp; workmanship standards, and ensuring blockers are cleared at the appropriate level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Function as the liaison between employees and management for solving problems or addressing general questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist supervisor in coaching, mentoring, and training team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that all team members follow proper procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide information on specific materials and components required for tooling work orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technician GSE support, which involves building, installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting pneumatic and hydraulic equipment such as valves, plumbing, and components related to the Starship Tower build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain, troubleshoot, and repair equipment and instrumentation as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read and interpret planning documents, schematics, specifications, drawings, manuals, blueprints, and engineering sketches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and maintain hardware, high-pressure systems, and other ancillary equipment, including mechanical, pneumatic, and hydraulic components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fabricate and repair GSE/testing hardware and equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with design engineers to develop and document GSE/testing activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Obtain and maintain licenses, operator permits, or certifications as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow all necessary regulations and appropriate SpaceX procedures, including quality policies, safety policies, OSHA, EPA, NIOSH, NFPA, ASME, NEC, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop novel ways site-wide to streamline processes and increase the reliability of testing operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive workspace cleanliness; maintain organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform a variety of related duties in support of integrated system installation and activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of industrial experience such as installing pipes and components, bending stainless tubes, or working around high-pressure systems (pneumatic or hydraulic)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years assembling and configuring large mechanical structures and test stands using forklifts, cranes, and proper rigging techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A&amp;amp;P license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the aerospace industry, military, or other high-reliability operating environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in ground support equipment in the aerospace industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical aptitude and experience (work with machines and general tooling)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formalized mechanical training, skilled in hand and power tool usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn/experience troubleshooting and repairing instrumentation and low-voltage wiring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience where quick-thinking and problem-solving play a critical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of all types of borescope inspection equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of different fittings such as NPT and A/N&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to utilize power tools and hand tools as well as heavy equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use of precision measuring instruments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and understand mechanical and electrical schematics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of hazardous systems – cryogenic, flammable, hypergolic, pyrophoric&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of high-pressure system design and handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General physical fitness is required for some work areas, as flight hardware typically is built in tight quarters, and physical dexterity is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work the following shift:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monday – Friday 6:00 am – 4:30 pm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license and a clean driving record&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work at elevated heights up to 500ft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel to alternate work sites to support fabrication activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically exposed to work in extreme outdoor environments – heat, cold, rain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work overtime and weekends depending on site operational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to pass an Air Force background check for Cape Canaveral&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand: Up to 10 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit: Up to 3 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push/Pull: Up to 75lbs. (unassisted) 1-2 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overhead reach: Up to 10 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Walk: Up to 10 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lift/Carry: Up to 50lbs. (unassisted) 1-2 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Climb (ladder/stairs): Up to 6 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kneel/Crouch: Up to 10 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upper body twist: Up to 6 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in temperatures over 80 degrees for 6 hours or more per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidate must be capable of safely working at heights (up to 500ft), in confined spaces, operating heavy equipment and machinery, and performing the physical requirements of the job listed in the job description&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidate may be required to complete a pre-employment questionnaire and/or physical to confirm these capabilities, which may include a medical history review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
