&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LEAD MECHANICAL ENGINEER, MEP (TEXAS CONSTRUCTION PROJECTS)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As lead mechanical engineer, MEP, on the Texas Construction Projects team, you will provide technical leadership and direction to engineers across multiple disciplines in the design, construction, and activation of critical infrastructure that enables SpaceX to achieve its long-term mission. You will own the successful delivery of large capital projects for internal customer groups across the company, drive technical decisions, mentor team members, and ensure projects meet performance, schedule, and quality objectives. This position is based in McGregor, TX (Waco area). Travel may be required, and based on business needs, opportunities to support other SpaceX facilities may arise in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership and direction to the project team, consulting engineers, and contractors throughout the full lifecycle of mechanical, electrical, and plumbing (MEP) engineering, procurement, construction, and commissioning for large capital projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the development and issuance of engineering drawings, design documentation, and technical reports for aerospace, industrial, and commercial infrastructure projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the preparation, negotiation, and management of construction contracts with subcontractors across multiple disciplines, from initial award through final close-out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the real-time resolution of complex design and construction conflicts in the field, ensuring minimal impact to schedule and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead coordination efforts with electrical utility providers on design and engineering activities to ensure reliable and resilient power delivery to critical site infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary technical interface with engineers, contractors, fabricators, and key project stakeholders, fostering alignment and driving successful project outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, or other engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional experience with the design or build of MEP building systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of leadership experience leading teams, projects, or people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Primary experience with electrical and power distribution systems (&amp;lt;600Vac)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of HVAC operation and design principles including refrigeration, chillers, boilers, and air-handling equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with plumbing design and operation including domestic water, wastewater, venting, and storm systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of delta/wye transformers, building lighting, building construction specifications, and facility grounding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with critical power infrastructure including UPS systems, backup generators, and automatic transfer switches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and implementing process/design solutions with minimal impact to business operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to quickly assess an issue and assist technicians with troubleshooting and repair&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a high-concentration, high-stress environment, under possible extended work hours and tight deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acute attention to detail, ability to see interactions with other systems to avoid problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AutoCAD/Revit – Beginner to intermediate skill level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with National Electric Code, ASHRAE, National Fire Protection Association, and International Building Code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role may require extended hours, weekend work and shift schedules, that vary depending on site operational needs; flexibility required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role requires you to be onsite - remote or hybrid work will NOT be considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform hands-on work in all environments (heat, cold, rain), in tight quarters or at heights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain focused while working in hazardous environments while wearing appropriate PPE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
