&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working as an electrical engineer focusing on power distribution systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineering license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with electrical and power distribution systems of high, medium, and low voltage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and implementing process/design solutions without shutting down or pausing business operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and installing systems in a Class 1, Division 1 and Division 2 environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acute attention to detail, ability to see interactions with other systems to avoid problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with National Electric Code, National Fire Protection Association and International Building Code analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substations (utility company)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switchgear and motor control centers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Primary (12,470Vac) and secondary (480/277Vac) power distribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delta/Wye transformer configurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Panel circuit assignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Load center balancing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building lighting, building construction specifications, and facility grounding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combination motor starters, Variable Frequency Drives, electrical motor troubleshooting/repair&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AutoCAD - Intermediate skill level (AutoCAD Electrical a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UPS systems, Backup Generators, Automatic Transfer Switches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
