&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MAINTENANCE MANAGER (POWER PLANT)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceX is seeking a Power Plant Maintenance Manager to own the maintenance, equipment reliability, and long-term asset performance of power generation infrastructure supporting the Starbase supercomputer. This position will lead maintenance execution across gas turbines, generators, rotating equipment, mechanical and electrical balance-of-plant systems, and associated industrial utilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate is an experienced power plant engineer who understands how equipment fails, how to prevent repeat failures, and how to execute maintenance without compromising plant availability. You will build and lead a maintenance organization, develop preventive and predictive maintenance strategies, coordinate major outages, and work directly with technicians, engineers, and equipment manufacturers to maximize equipment reliability. This is a hands-on leadership role requiring technical depth, strong planning, and the ability to solve problems in the field.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Lead and develop the power plant maintenance organization, including mechanical, electrical, instrumentation, and controls maintenance personnel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Own preventive, predictive, and corrective maintenance programs for gas turbines, generators, pumps, motors, compressors, valves, cooling systems, and associated balance-of-plant equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Develop and execute maintenance plans and inspection schedules based on OEM recommendations, equipment condition, operating history, and reliability requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Plan and manage major turbine maintenance activities, including combustion inspections, hot gas path inspections, overhauls, and associated plant outages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Direct root cause investigations for recurring equipment failures, turbine trips, vibration issues, lubrication failures, and other mechanical or electrical problems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Implement condition-monitoring and predictive maintenance tools including vibration analysis, thermography, oil analysis, and equipment performance trending&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Establish and maintain a computerized maintenance management system (CMMS), including equipment histories, preventive maintenance schedules, work orders, and maintenance backlog tracking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Develop spare parts strategies, critical inventory requirements, maintenance budgets, and vendor support agreements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Work directly with turbine OEMs, equipment suppliers, and contractors to resolve technical issues, coordinate repairs, and maintain equipment reliability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Coordinate maintenance work with plant operations to minimize downtime, ensure safe equipment isolation, and support timely return to service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Support installation, commissioning, maintenance readiness, and turnover of new power generation assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Establish maintenance performance metrics, including planned maintenance compliance, equipment availability, repeat failure rates, and mean time to repair&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Ensure maintenance execution complies with applicable safety requirements, including lockout/tagout, electrical safety, hot work, confined-space entry, and equipment isolation procedure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related engineering discipline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;5+ years of hands-on experience in power plant maintenance, rotating equipment reliability, or maintenance engineering at a power generation facility&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience planning and executing maintenance on gas turbines, generators, or associated industrial plant equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience leading maintenance personnel, contractors, or multidisciplinary technical work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Direct maintenance experience with gas turbines, generators, steam turbines, and mechanical/electrical balance-of-plant systems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience with GE, Siemens Energy, Mitsubishi Power, or comparable turbine OEM equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of rotating equipment, bearings, seals, lubrication systems, alignment, vibration analysis, and equipment failure modes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience planning and executing turbine inspections, hot gas path maintenance, major overhauls, and forced outage repairs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Proficiency with CMMS platforms, maintenance scheduling, equipment asset management, and critical spare parts inventory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience implementing preventive, predictive, and reliability-centered maintenance programs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead root cause failure analysis and implement permanent corrective actions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Familiarity with long-term service agreements, warranty administration, maintenance contracts, and OEM technical support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience working with industrial electrical systems, motors, generators, switchgear, PLCs, and instrumentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Ability to interpret P&amp;amp;IDs, mechanical drawings, electrical schematics, and equipment maintenance manuals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience supporting new plant construction, commissioning, and equipment turnover into maintenance programs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Knowledge of industrial maintenance safety requirements, including OSHA practices, NFPA 70E, and lockout/tagout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Demonstrated improvements in equipment availability, maintenance cost, outage duration, or recurring failure rates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Must be able to work onsite at Starbase, TX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Must be available to support critical equipment failures, outages, and maintenance events outside standard business hours&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Must be willing to work extended hours and weekends during major maintenance activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Ability to work in industrial environments, including outdoors, around rotating machinery, and in confined spaces or elevated locations when necessary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Ability to wear required personal protective equipment and safely access equipment for inspections and troubleshooting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Willingness to travel to OEM facilities or other project sites as needed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MAINTENANCE ENGINEER, PCB (STARLINK)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SpaceX we’re leveraging our experience in building rockets and spacecraft to deploy Starlink, the world’s most advanced broadband internet system. Starlink is the world’s largest satellite constellation and is providing fast, reliable internet to 10M+ users worldwide. We design, build, test, and operate all parts of the system – thousands of satellites, consumer receivers that allow users to connect within minutes of unboxing, and the software that brings it all together. We’ve only begun to scratch the surface of Starlink’s potential global impact and are looking for best-in-class engineers to help maximize Starlink’s utility for communities and businesses around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The primary role of the Maintenance Engineer is to identify and manage asset reliability risks that could adversely affect factory or business operations. As production develops and increases rate, the Maintenance Engineer&#39;s primary goal is to achieve maximum asset and system up-time by implementing and executing plans to minimize production losses, unpredictable asset behavior, and unusually high costs for system maintainability. In addition, the Maintenance Engineer acts as the accountable engineering resource in driving the design, build, and installation stages of new and modified assets as well as provides technical support to maintenance management, technicians, and production personnel to prevent and mitigate operational issues of critical equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with project engineering to ensure the reliability and sustainability of new and modified installations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide efforts to ensure consistency and maintainability of critical equipment, processes, utilities, facilities, controls, and safety/security systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own equipment improvement plans for more responsive and developed preventative maintenance strategies, equipment effectiveness, and minimization of production downtime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, design, develop, monitor, and refine an asset maintenance plan that includes value-added preventive maintenance tasks, minimization of high-cost low-value repairs, effective utilization of predictive, and other non-destructive testing methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare asset documentation package for review of system mechanical design, controls, and software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop engineering solutions to repetitive failures and equipment-specific problems that adversely affect plant operations including capacity, quality, cost, or regulatory compliance issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with production to perform analyses of assets including asset utilization rate, overall equipment effectiveness, remaining useful life, operational restrictions, and other parameters that define the operating condition, reliability, and costs of assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support to production, maintenance management, and technical personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage production requests for asset improvement, control functions, and data collection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply value analysis to repair/replace, repair/redesign, and make/buy decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in mechanical, electrical, aerospace, systems, or manufacturing engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in an engineering role in manufacturing, integration, reliability, technical program management, and/or operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
