&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MAINTENANCE TECHNICIAN&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Self-sufficient, independent, all-round technician performing preventive and emergent maintenance and troubleshooting on various equipment used by the Flight Hardware Logistics team, which is responsible for the transportation of Falcon engines, stages, and components. We are looking for a systematic problem solver who understands a high-volume manufacturing environment and keeps the equipment running in optimal condition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and repair the following: air ride suspension and brake systems, lighting, wiring, gas-powered pony motors and generators, and fluid hydraulic systems on shipping fixtures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage in preventive maintenance of various mechanical, control, hydraulic, fluid, and electrical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot various mechanical, control, hydraulic, fluid, and electrical systems down to the component level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to the California Highway Patrol (CHP) Biennial Inspection of Terminals (BIT) and Department of Transportation (DOT) regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform CHP and DOT-required 90-day inspections, as well as annual inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document all work and repairs by creating and updating maintenance tickets and work orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional experience in maintaining, troubleshooting, or repairing electrical, mechanical, fluid, and/or control systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team or managing a maintenance program, shop, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to rapidly change roles/responsibilities while maintaining a high sense of urgency in a high-paced, challenging work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Microsoft Office (Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial driver’s license (CDL)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
