&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MANAGER, MACHINE MAINTENANCE – SOLAR CELL FACTORY (STARLINK)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SpaceX we are building the next generation of space infrastructure to enable large-scale AI data centers in orbit. These orbital AI platforms require massive amounts of reliable, high-efficiency solar power to support intensive computing workloads in space. To make this possible, we are standing up one of the largest solar cell manufacturing facilities in the world. We are seeking an experienced Machine Maintenance Manager to lead the ramp-up and sustained reliability of advanced production equipment and automation systems. This high-impact role offers the opportunity to build and shape the maintenance organization from the ground up while directly enabling SpaceX’s ambitious vision for AI data centers in space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a high-performing team of maintenance technicians and engineers responsible for 24/7 reliability of advanced solar cell production equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive maintenance strategies, including preventative, predictive, and corrective programs to achieve &amp;gt;95% equipment availability on critical lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee rapid troubleshooting, root cause analysis, and permanent corrective actions for complex systems including vacuum deposition, chemical processing, and automation equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Production and Facility Operations teams to integrate maintenance windows with factory schedules while minimizing impact on output targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage maintenance budgets, spare parts inventory, and strategic vendor relationships to optimize costs without compromising quality or reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives focused on increasing Overall Equipment Effectiveness (OEE) and supporting rapid factory scaling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strict adherence to safety protocols, cleanroom standards, and regulatory requirements during all maintenance activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of technical excellence, accountability, and innovation to enable SpaceX’s vision for AI data centers in space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering or STEM discipline; OR 5+ years of experience leading industrial maintenance teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience working in a manufacturing/operations environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a leadership position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of prior experience with semiconductor, solar, advanced automation, or other equipment maintenance and reliability programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record leading cross-functional teams in high-volume, fast-paced manufacturing environments under tight deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience maintaining solar cell production equipment, including thin-film deposition tools (PECVD, sputtering systems, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of electrical, mechanical, and pneumatic systems in highly automated production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Computerized Maintenance Management Systems (CMMS) and data analytics tools for equipment reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong familiarity with lean manufacturing principles, total productive maintenance, Six Sigma, or similar process improvement methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to scale maintenance programs in high-growth manufacturing environments, ideally in renewable energy aerospace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of cleanroom protocols and safe handling of pyrophoric and toxic gas systems during maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead and execute effectively in a fast-paced environment while maintaining high standards of quality and safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel internationally (20%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand up to 6 hours, lift up to 25 pounds unassisted, and maneuver around equipment in a factory setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in industrial environments with fumes/odors, noise, hazardous chemicals, and confined spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work all shifts, extended hours, and weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
