&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MANAGER, PRODUCTION (PRECISION TUBE FABRICATION)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Precision Tube Fabrication team is looking for a Production Manager to help lead our production operations. This is a fast-paced and high-volume manufacturing facility responsible for delivering finished fluid systems assemblies to our Falcon &amp;amp; Dragon customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depending on the skillset and technical knowledge of the candidate, the scope of the production manager role will encompass the following:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Back End Area&lt;/strong&gt; (proof &amp;amp; leak, cleaning, assembly, insulation, rework, bag &amp;amp; tag).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a staff of supervisors and 80+ employees across multiple shifts toward goals aligned to company targets for safety, quality, cost, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a strong focus is placed on safety and achieve excellent safety performance with the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage quality metrics to continually improve the output of the team; play a leading role in ensuring root cause for quality issues are identified and appropriate improvement actions are put in place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve cost targets by improving labor efficiency, eliminating rework/scrap drivers, and driving design for manufacturability improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the team to achieve ambitious delivery targets that support the company’s launch manifest, while continuing to uphold high quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the overall organization in the strategic planning of labor, equipment, facilities, and other resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, plan, and execute capital equipment, machine, and layout upgrades to meet volume production demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop high-performing leaders and inspire a culture of excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster an environment of continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think creatively and question the status quo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in an engineering discipline or 4+ years of experience in one or more of the following industries:&amp;nbsp;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manufacturing/production operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supply chain management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Military operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of leadership experience in manufacturing or production role with direct reports.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a leadership role with direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience within manufacturing operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong technical understanding and practical knowledge of fluid systems manufacturing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively communicate with all levels in the organization, including production technicians, engineering, and the Executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing team performance metrics, setting targets, and driving production teams to achieve those targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to adapt to constantly changing work assignments and a fast-paced work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent attention to detail with outstanding work efficiency and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly motivated and team-oriented leader with strong communication skills and ability to work with cross-functional teams within the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with applying lean manufacturing principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated record of high-performance (rated 4/4 or above in previous review cycles).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work long hours and weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to lift a minimum of 25 lbs. unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pay Range:&lt;br&gt;$140,000.00 - $190,000.00&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of your total rewards package at SpaceX. You may also be eligible for long-term incentives, in the form of company stock or long-term cash awards, as well as potential discretionary bonuses and the ability to purchase additional stock at a discount through an Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You will also receive access to comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, paid parental leave, and various other discounts and perks. You may also accrue 3 weeks of paid vacation and will be eligible for 10 or more paid holidays per year. Employees accrue paid sick leave pursuant to Company policy which satisfies or exceeds the accrual, carryover, and use requirements of the law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;MANAGER, SEMICONDUCTOR SOURCING (STARLINK)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;We are seeking an experienced leader to own end-to-end sourcing strategy, supplier management, and delivery of leading-edge semiconductor components. In this role, you will partner directly with design engineering to define commodity strategy, build multi-year technology roadmaps, establish and maintain the approved vendor list, and secure massive-scale supply at the record-breaking build speeds Starlink is driving. You will lead a team to negotiate transformative, high-value agreements, accelerate delivery timelines, actively manage inventory across the supply chain, and continuously optimize for cost, quality, speed, and supply chain resilience in the most competitive and dynamic programs on the planet. The ideal candidate is a strategic leader who thrives in ambiguous, high-velocity environments, possesses exceptional commercial and technical acumen, and has a proven track record of leading teams to deliver excellent results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Lead a team of sourcing specialists, sourcing managers, and/or global supply managers to ensure continuity of supply for all hardware within the scope of ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Drive improvement, standardization, and scalability of operational planning, workflow, tools, and resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Assess employee performance, provide positive and constructive feedback, facilitate conflict resolution, and address repeat issues with corrective actions, performance improvement plans, or disciplinary means&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Own vision and strategy for assigned categories through NPI and production phases; methods may include, but are not limited to cost management, contract negotiations, supplier development, supplier performance management, industry research, and long-term strategic sourcing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Visit supplier facilities and accurately assess operational capability, financial health, and capacity in order to award contracts in support of new product development and long-term production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Conduct comprehensive supplier analysis, including strategic direction, capacity, market and industry position, and risk assessment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders to define service level agreements (SLAs) and key performance indicators (KPIs) for suppliers and evaluate performance across critical metrics such as business outcomes, cost savings, quality, and delivery timeliness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Present value propositions to SpaceX executives, including those related to contract awards, cost reviews, cost reduction strategies, and critical supply issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Provide guidance to internal customers on design for manufacturability and trade analysis for mechanical components and assemblies, onboarding requirements, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Ensure partners are prepared to support all prototype builds with appropriate equipment and materials for successful product development, ramp-up, and production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Negotiate long-term contracts to ensure continuity of supply and protect SpaceX interests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree and 6+ years of experience in one or more of the following, or 10+ years of experience in one or more of the following in lieu of a degree:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Purchasing or procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Material or production planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Operations or supply chain management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Master production scheduling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;3+ years of experience in a management role with direct reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Experience sharing information and influencing others across organizational lines, internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to make presentations to suppliers, team members, internal customers, and senior management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Demonstrated exceptional achievements at SpaceX and/or previous companies to execute improvement projects quickly, while maintaining product reliability and mission success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Experience directly negotiating contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Experience sourcing suppliers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Prior formal people leadership experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Organized and self-driven, capable of working independently with little direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Ability to conduct all activities with integrity and urgency&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Must be able to travel for short and extended trips as needed; up to 50%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Must be able to work long hours and weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Must be able to work onsite in Redmond, WA. Remote work is not considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pay Range:&lt;br&gt;$145,000.00 - $205,000.00&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of your total rewards package at SpaceX. You may also be eligible for long-term incentives, in the form of company stock or long-term cash awards, as well as potential discretionary bonuses and the ability to purchase additional stock at a discount through an Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You will also receive access to comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, paid parental leave, and various other discounts and perks. You may also accrue 3 weeks of paid vacation and will be eligible for 10 or more paid holidays per year. Employees in Washington State accrue paid sick time in compliance with state and federal law. Company shuttles are offered to employees for roundtrip travel from select Seattle locations to the SpaceX Redmond office Monday to Friday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
