&lt;li&gt;Represent supplier development engineering in Starship program forums; ensure supply chain has a seat at the table and alignment with Starship program priorities by establishing trust with senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive and motivate managers and teams to ensure all deliverables and expectations are met and executed, with quick decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reporting procedures and systems to inform and align on reliability progress, help needed, and opportunities for improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement process, system, or training improvement projects with tangible results, and effectively delegate execution across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and review established KPIs with managers and teams, and adjust initiatives as needed to drive progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and champion cross-functional technical cost-reduction efforts and projects in collaboration with sourcing leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work autonomously and proactively to resolve a wide variety of potentially ambiguous issues in creative, resourceful ways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the organization has both a high-level and granular understanding of quality risk across the Starship program, and drive collaboration to broadly reduce quality risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the supplier development engineering roadmap for Starship flight hardware, including structures, propulsion, avionics, fluids, and related commodities as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and scale a world-class supplier development engineering organization, including people managers and individual contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct weekly 1:1s with direct reports (including managers) and collaborate on personal development plans for each member&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach managers on hiring, performance management, and developing their teams; hold the leadership bench accountable to results and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview and hire candidates for Supply Chain with a strong eye for talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a succession plan with leads and managers and effectively manage attrition to ensure business continuity, while growing and developing individual contributors into future leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embody and radiate best practices in team collaboration, respect, transparency, and team problem solving with a high sense of integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
