&lt;li&gt;Responsible for implementing plug-and-play processes to production that are capable of high volume throughput (1M+ per year)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take direct ownership of the physical production layout, optimizing for material flow from material receiving through processes on the line&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement safety improvement projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage strategy for production line tooling, inventory, training, and build process and ensure all are updated according to the latest design configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive design for test (DFT) best practices and design for manufacturing (DFM) with design engineers and test engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify automation opportunities and establish requirements as well as evaluating return on investment for each&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with in-house resources or vendors as necessary to develop these solutions and implement on production line&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support production line with technical issues that cannot be addressed immediately on the line&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
