&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills (written and oral)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior Riggers License - FAA (Federal Aviation Administration) or military equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with parachute systems (large or cargo canopies preferred, and/or pressure packing canopies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with textiles (cord, webbing, tape, broadcloth, and thread) and the ability to interpret technical drawings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a quality department or in quality training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-consequence, meticulous procedural work (e.g., FAA Airframe and Powerplant (A&amp;amp;P) certificate or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of quality assurance principles, methods, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-resolution inspection photography&lt;/li&gt;
