&lt;p&gt;Physical Security Specialists are highly experienced and adaptable security professionals who operate with significant autonomy in dynamic, high-threat environments. This position is responsible for providing advanced protective and operational support across SpaceX facilities and executive movements. Specialists are expected to operate as an individual or small team, make independent decisions in the field, and deliver executive-level protection while conducting reconnaissance, counter-surveillance, and border proximity security operations. This position requires a flexible schedule driven by threat trends and company commitments rather than fixed shifts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct executive protection operations and provide close protection for senior leadership as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform reconnaissance and counter-surveillance in support of executive movements and threat mitigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead small teams during operations while also demonstrating the ability to work independently and make sound decisions with limited oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the planning and execution of security for large-scale company events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct advanced risk assessments and develop mitigation strategies for critical assets and personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain proficiency in advanced protective tactics, surveillance detection, mobile operations and emergency medicine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a liaison with law enforcement agencies and key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to and manage incidents with professionalism and sound judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate small utility vehicles, drones and watercraft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in the military, law enforcement, overseas security contracting, or advanced corporate security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of executive protection, mobile asset protection, or emergency response team experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or advanced degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified Peace Officer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Unit Operations or SWAT certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HR218 credentials (or equivalent authorization) permitting the carrying of firearms in all United States jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combat medic, EMT-B, paramedic, or advanced medical emergency training (TCCC/TECC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting executive protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning security for large-scale events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting reconnaissance and counter-surveillance operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience de-escalating disputes and manage conflict professionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience instructing security tactics, operations, and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documented small unit leadership or team management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Military deployment and/or counterinsurgency experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication skills with the ability to interface effectively with executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foreign language proficiency (Spanish)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
