&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRODUCTION SHIFT SUPERVISOR (STARLINK/AKOUSTIS)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Akoustis is now operating as a wholly owned subsidiary of SpaceX providing industry leading RF filters using patented XBAW technology to help drive the mission of making human life multi-planetary, while also connecting the world through Starlink. Our work helps further the impact that Starlink is already making on millions of users around the world, while allowing us to broaden that reach dramatically and continue connecting the unconnected here on earth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position supports RF filter production for SpaceX’s Starlink satellite internet constellation and growing defense communications portfolio. An Akoustis Production Shift Supervisor manages operators and production technicians to support manufacturing processes to improve yield, quality, and efficiency that set new standards in bulk acoustic wave (BAW) filter performance. They lead cross functional teams to meet work center goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead daily operations for assigned production area and ensures operators and technicians meet daily output targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage shift schedules and overtime to maintain required staffing levels and meet production commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report weekly KPI performance to management and drives corrective actions when metrics fall below targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and prioritize high-volume production schedules to meet customer delivery dates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cycle time reduction and continuous improvement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and closes corrective and preventive actions (CAPAs) within defined timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive equipment uptime improvement initiatives in collaboration with maintenance and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve process integration issues across work centers to reduce scrap and rework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce safety and quality protocols and leads daily safety and quality reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage work-in-process (WIP) levels across work centers to meet cycle time goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain chemical inventory accuracy and ensures uninterrupted material availability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-train operators across work centers to improve flexibility and reduce bottlenecks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead yield improvement efforts and implements actions to reduce scrap and increase first-pass yield&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cost reduction projects and 5S initiatives to improve efficiency and workplace organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate’s degree and 3+ years of professional experience in a manufacturing or test environment; OR high school diploma or equivalency certificate and 5+ years of professional experience in a manufacturing or test environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a supervisory or team lead position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience working in the semiconductor, electronics, or manufacturing industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or higher in a semiconductor or science-related field such as materials science, chemical engineering, electrical engineering, microelectronics, nanotechnology, chemistry, or physics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in JMP and Microsoft Office Suite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in semiconductor fabrication processes and statistical process control&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in at least one fab process area (photolithography, deposition, etch, or test)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading projects that improved process development or yield&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with metrology and failure analysis techniques&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
