&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALITY SPECIALIST (STARSHIP)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Quality Specialist is a hands-on shop-floor role on Starship, focused on MRB, FOD and tool control, measurement, and cleanliness. You will process non-conforming hardware from receipt through disposition and outbound flow. Additional responsibilities include training production on Issue Tickets and working with the Build Reliability Engineering (BRE) team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive MRB hardware from Incoming, stage it on racks, and process it through MRB&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review Issue Tickets and rejection paperwork on receipt; get senders to fix bad info or wrong routing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate logistics with on-site and off-site teams for nonconforming material delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get dispositions from Engineering (Repair, Use As Is, Scrap &amp;amp; Destroy, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep outgoing hardware moving to workcenters, other sites for rework, or scrap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process hardware with laptops, cameras, and iPads; paint, tag, remove stickers, and apply scrap markings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep documentation and tracking accurate; audit Issue Tickets for rationale, deviation docs, and disposition verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help quarantine suspect product and update production leadership on containment and disposition status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and audit FOD and tool control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use measurement tools and devices for inspection and verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cleanliness inspectors on criteria, measurement, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write simple visual instructions when needed (test plans, OP instructions, infographics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train production on Issue Tickets, documentation, and repeat failures/escapes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the BRE team on quality issues and inspection methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in an engineering, manufacturing, or quality field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in quality, inspection, MRB, non-conformance processing, or manufacturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FOD and tool control experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on use of measurement tools and devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong computer skills (laptops, iPads, cameras, and digital systems)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, PowerPoint)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working hands-on with hardware (painting, labeling, sticker removal, physical organization of parts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forklift experience (SpaceX will train and qualify)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with Engineering, senders, and material handlers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can explain work with simple visual instructions (test plans, OP instructions, infographics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret design drawings and CAD models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AS9100, ISO 9001, or similar QMS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of quality tools such as root cause analysis, corrective action, and problem-solving methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 25 lbs. unassisted and to stand for extended periods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flight hardware typically is built at height or in tight quarters, and physical dexterity is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform job duties that require standing, kneeling, crouching, twisting upper body, working in cramped positions in small openings, and climbing hand over hand&lt;/li&gt;
