&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Enterprise or complex B2B sales motions (ideally technology, SaaS, telecom, satellite/connectivity, or hardware)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to facilitate role-plays, workshops, and certifications that change seller behavior—not only present slides&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining an enablement content library (pitch decks, one-pagers, playbooks, LMS/modules) with strong version control and field-facing quality bar&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering or supporting partner/reseller enablement sessions and tracking certification completion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with CRM and enablement tooling (HubSpot or Salesforce; LMS, content portals, or similar)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to turn product and process updates into clear, practical training&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized operator mindset: calendars, logistics, cohort tracking, and follow-through in a high-volume environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth, fast-paced environments with frequent product and GTM changes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with onboarding/ramp programs (30/60/90) and everboarding cadences is a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Grok Build is a plus&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to work extended hours and/or weekends as needed to support onboarding cohorts, product launches, partner enablement events, or critical sales initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel as needed to support training delivery, partner sessions, and key field events&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
