&lt;p&gt;Starlink is the world’s largest satellite constellation delivering high-speed, low-latency broadband to customers around the globe. As the Sales Operations Lead on the Starlink Enterprise team, you will be the hands-on trainer and program executor who turns enablement strategy into delivered results for sellers, account managers, and resellers. You will facilitate workshops and role-plays, keep the content library current, run partner enablement sessions, and close feedback loops so every training event improves the next one—raising the skill bar across the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and facilitate live workshops, role-plays, and certification sessions for Enterprise sellers and account managers; support the structured 30/60/90-day onboarding experience by running key training sessions and tracking completion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day management of the enablement content library—pitch decks, one-pagers, playbooks, and training materials—so assets stay current after product, pricing, process, and messaging changes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver partner and reseller enablement sessions in coordination with Channel Operations and the Sales Enablement Manager; track certification completion and session attendance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture field feedback after every session and feed clear improvements back to the Sales Enablement Manager, Channel Operations, and content owners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with SMEs (Product, SE, Sales Ops, Channel) to prepare session agendas, demos, and practice scenarios that map to priority GTM workflows—not generic soft-skills training&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain enablement calendars, logistics, and delivery readiness for cohort onboarding, everboarding, and partner programs so launches and training waves run on time&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help measure enablement effectiveness (attendance, certification completion, post-session feedback, asset usage) and surface gaps that should inform the next enablement cycle&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a reliable operator for the field: consistent delivery quality, fast asset turnaround, and scalable capacity so the Sales Enablement Manager can focus on program design and prioritization&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in sales enablement, learning &amp;amp; development, sales training, revenue operations support, or a related go-to-market function&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience facilitating live training, workshops, or certification sessions for sales or customer-facing teams&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
