&lt;li&gt;Responsible for tracking special events and visits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide high-quality customer service to employees, contractors, and visitors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure thorough knowledge and effective implementation of all access control, escort, and tour protocols and procedures for employees, customers, vendors, and guests at SpaceX facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Security leadership and the SpaceX Protective Operations Center (SPOC) as necessary to:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate timely and effective notifications and response measures for incidents or emergencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist emergency response personnel dispatched to a SpaceX site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor site surveillance camera system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear and concise written incident reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report maintenance, facility, and technology issues and alarms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build collaborative working relationships with other SpaceX departments or teams (including, but not limited to, Facilities, Human Resources, and Employee Health &amp;amp;amp; Safety), SpaceX leadership, and—where applicable—with landlords and building owners, regarding day-to-day security operations, as well as special events or emergency situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Due to the various type and scope of operations performed and sites utilized at SpaceX, Security Operator responsibilities may vary at each campus in order to ensure the most effective and secure operations at all sites. This may include, but is not limited to: standing post, escort duty, tours, and various tasks as directed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
