&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SR. AUTOMATION &amp;amp; CONTROLS ENGINEER (ASSET ENGINEERING)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Asset Engineering team is dedicated to developing the factory machines, tooling, and systems required to manufacture some of the most advanced hardware on the planet. With vertically integrated teams of mechanical, automation, and fluids engineers, the group solves SpaceX&#39;s most difficult manufacturing challenges, owning the solutions from design concept though high-rate production ramps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sr. Automation and Controls Engineer, you will be directly responsible for the design, build, and integration of automated machinery that manufactures and tests Starship and Starshield hardware. You will join a highly talented interdisciplinary team of engineers and technicians working to ensure the Hawthorne factory unlocks its full capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;design and&amp;nbsp;development&amp;nbsp;of complex&amp;nbsp;in-house&amp;nbsp;automated manufacturing and test systems from concept to production, specifically owning electrical and software design.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop motion control and&amp;nbsp;robotic&amp;nbsp;systems to&amp;nbsp;solve manufacturing and test needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;maintain&amp;nbsp;machine automation software that is concise and well documented.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop&amp;nbsp;simple&amp;nbsp;UI /&amp;nbsp;HMIs&amp;nbsp;that&amp;nbsp;make machines easy to understand,&amp;nbsp;operate&amp;nbsp;and troubleshoot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design&amp;nbsp;electrical&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;pneumatic&amp;nbsp;systems&amp;nbsp;to be used in manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the build, integration,&amp;nbsp;testing&amp;nbsp;and validation&amp;nbsp;of electrical and fluidic systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and implement the integration of&amp;nbsp;manufacturing machinery into SCADA and MES systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide expert support of existing automation systems and work with partner teams to correct root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in engineering, physics, computer&amp;nbsp;science&amp;nbsp;or other engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in industrial or factory automation design and implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in designing and building electro-mechanical/robotic/automated system products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
