&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SR. IT WIRELESS NETWORK ENGINEER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is looking for an experienced wireless network engineer with a strong background in designing, deploying and managing wireless networks in an enterprise environment. This employee will be a member of the Network Engineering team, which is responsible for managing SpaceX’s wireless networks across all sites. This network supports the designing, manufacturing and launching of rockets, spacecraft, satellites as well as human space flight. The position will be heavily focused on designing, building and troubleshooting wireless networks. The ideal candidate will be a great communicator, able to document work, excel at multi-tasking and enjoy a fast-paced high-tech environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design access point placements for new wireless network deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the network infrastructure team to ensure access points are deployed in desired locations and to our standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform wireless surveys to identify coverage gaps/performance concerns and implement remediation efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot wireless issues across a large enterprise deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule and perform software and hardware updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Procure and manage wireless hardware inventory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor wireless network health using in-house and 3rd party tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain proper documentation of our wireless networks across all sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, computer engineering, or other engineering discipline and 5+ of years professional network engineering experience; OR 7+ years of professional network engineering experience in lieu of a degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert understanding of wireless/RF technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CBRS deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with the following:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cisco wireless LAN controllers or other wireless technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cisco DNA Center.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ekahau wireless products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network monitoring tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux/Windows system administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry standard certifications such as CCNA, CCNP, or CCIE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work extended hours, nights and weekends when needed to meet critical deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have valid driver&#39;s license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to pass Air Force background check for Vandenberg and Cape Canaveral.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical effort including standing, lifting and carrying moderately heavy materials (up to 25 lbs unassisted) or equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally exposed to work in extreme outdoor environments – heat, cold, rain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work occasionally performed in an environment requiring exposure to fumes, odors, and noise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work at elevated heights and/or tight spaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as required to common destinations including Hawthorne, CA; McGregor, TX; Vandenberg, CA; Cape Canaveral, FL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
