&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SENIOR MANAGER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is building and operating combined-cycle gas turbine power plants that must come online, stay online, and perform. This role owns the design and build of the full power plant: gas turbines, mechanical and electrical balance of plant, and everything else that keeps the plant running at rated output, day after day. This is not a desk job. You will be constructing the power plant, owning commissioning in the control room during startup, and in the field troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and develop a multi-disciplinary power plant team spanning gas turbines, mechanical and electrical balance of plant, controls, and commissioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full lifecycle of gas turbine power generation assets — installation, commissioning, startup, operations, and long-term maintenance — and be accountable for plant availability, reliability, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction and execution plans for commissioning, including combustion tuning, control system checkout, protective relay testing, and performance/reliability run verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own root-cause analysis and corrective action for turbine trips, forced outages, and performance degradation; drive fixes that prevent recurrence and hold the team to a no-repeat standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and continuously improve operating procedures, startup/shutdown sequences, and abnormal operating condition playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary technical and commercial interface with OEMs (GE, Siemens Energy, Mitsubishi Power, Doosan) on warranty issues, LTSA scope, outage planning, and technical issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, staff, and execute major/minor inspections, hot gas path outages, and combustion inspections in line with OEM maintenance intervals; own outage cost, duration, and quality of return-to-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive turbine performance analysis (heat rate, capacity factor, degradation curves) to identify efficiency losses and convert findings into funded corrective action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate across balance-of-plant teams (HRSG, steam turbine, cooling systems, water treatment) to deliver integrated plant performance, not siloed subsystem success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the construction-to-operations handoff with EPC contractors; ensure a clean transition from construction to commercial operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and own spare parts strategy, critical spares inventory, and maintenance budgets; manage spend against reliability and availability targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach, and retain engineers and technicians; set performance standards and grow the next generation of plant leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the power plant organization to internal stakeholders (operations, grid interconnection, commercial, construction) and make timely field decisions under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree and 10+ years of experience working in one or more of the following; or 14+ years of experience working utility-scale gas turbines in commissioning, operations, maintenance, or plant engineering roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of project management experience leading operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of combined-cycle plant systems: gas turbines, HRSGs, steam turbines, generators, and balance-of-plant equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reading and interpreting P&amp;amp;IDs, single-line diagrams, and turbine control logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct commissioning or operations leadership experience with GE 7/9HA, Siemens Energy SGT6/8-8000H, Mitsubishi M501/701JAC, or Doosan H-class turbines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with DCS/turbine control platforms (Mark VIe, SPPA-T3000, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LTSA structures, OEM contract negotiation, and outage scope development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in root-cause failure analysis (RCA/5-Why/Fishbone) for rotating equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance monitoring tools and heat balance modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to grid interconnection requirements, PPA performance obligations, or capacity market rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating power generation with co-located industrial or data center loads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ownership of plant or fleet reliability metrics (availability, forced outage rate, heat rate) and of the budgets that fund them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up a new plant, commissioning organization, or operations team from construction through commercial operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward action: comfortable making a call in the field without waiting for a committee&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work under pressure during startup, outages, or unplanned events, with a sense of urgency and ownership over outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using SOLIDWORKS, Siemens NX, or similar CAD software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of engineering standards and best practices such as ASME B31.3, ASME BPV Code Section VIII, and AFSPCMAN 91-710&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SR. MANAGER, PRODUCT GROWTH STRATEGY (STARLINK)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Starlink is scaling consumer broadband worldwide. As Sr. Manager, Product Growth Strategy, you will lead the Starlink product growth team that takes service programs and offering changes to market, and you will be accountable for their growth impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team owns how we deploy programs such as plan and offer mechanics, referral programs, and market-specific value proposition work. You plan and product selection experiences and service programs work for markets, in partnership with global go-to-market teams. You organize how we ship changes to the product offering, new features, and new functionality across the service suite: launch coordination, impact planning, and prioritization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direction comes from Consumer Growth leadership, the broader growth team, and go-to-market. This is not an order-taking seat. The team is expected to bring ideas, justify them, vet them, test them, and take them to market. The work is high impact and closely reviewed. You need to be strong enough to stand behind the choices the team makes, read back in-market performance, and iterate or stop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the product growth team: set the bar, assign ownership, and hold the team to launch quality, timeline, and growth impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own how service programs and offering changes go to market (multi-family, community access, cash referral, market-specific value propositions, and similar programs), including what is in the offer, where it launches, and what GTM needs in each market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize deployment of product offering changes, new features, and new functionality across the service suite: roadmap, sequencing, launch coordination, and readiness with product, engineering, marketing, and in-market GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global go-to-market teams so online experiences and service programs actually work in market (positioning, eligibility, in-store activation, onboarding, ops handoff, and local constraints)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive impact planning and prioritization: size the growth case, sequence work against Consumer Growth goals, and kill or re-scope what will not move the number&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for program and offering growth impact: get work executed, read back performance after launch, and use that feedback to iterate, scale, or stop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a point of view. Source ideas, justify them with data and GTM input, vet feasibility, run tests, and take winners to market. Do not wait to be assigned a list&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent product growth in Consumer Growth and GTM forums: defend the plan, surface tradeoffs early, and keep US and in-market teams aligned through launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in product, growth, go-to-market, consumer programs, or a related role in a technical or consumer business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of direct people leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in product growth, consumer subscription, telecommunications, broadband, or marketplace businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years leading a team that shipped programs or product changes into market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of launch coordination across product, engineering, marketing, and in-country GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking service plans, promotions, or packaging changes live, then reading impact and iterating or killing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making digital purchase and onboarding experiences work across multiple countries or languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with market-specific value proposition work (including high-context markets such as Japan)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical chops: sizing, prioritization, experiment design, and post-launch readouts (Excel required; SQL or BI tools preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, high-scrutiny environment where you are expected to have a point of view and stand behind it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as needed to support global go-to-market teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work extended hours and weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SR. MANAGER, PURCHASING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a progressive procurement organization pushing the boundaries of traditional procurement reputation and methodologies. We are looking for individuals who can think outside the box to achieve company objectives regarding value and partnerships with our suppliers. Our organization moves quickly, and you must too. SpaceX has the unique ability and desire to influence and shape suppliers to be better with us as we challenge our supply chain on cost, quality and delivery. This individual will support indirect supplier management and SG&amp;amp;A spend reduction initiatives. The purchasing team has aggressive objectives for 2026 that will positively impact our product and bottom line. We are looking for the right person who is equipped and ready for these challenges to join our team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage the indirect purchasing team while setting strategic direction and vision for the cloud, software, services, and facilities categories across all SpaceX locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with internal stakeholders, deeply understand their needs, and partner with them to develop high-quality procurement strategies aligned to business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor who challenges stakeholders (including engineering and operations) to make decisions that support a high-performing, cost-effective supply plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own contract management to ensure supplier performance against obligations, drive on-time delivery, expedite as needed, and rapidly respond to demand changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute sourcing strategies that reduce risk, deliver continuous cost reduction, and align with company goals on payment terms, cash targets, on-time delivery, and savings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct comprehensive supplier and market analysis to build strategic sourcing plans that identify new/suitable suppliers, optimize cost structures, and proactively ensure supply continuity based on macro market and industry trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present clear value propositions to SpaceX executives covering contract awards, cost reviews, cost-reduction strategies, and critical supply issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement new tools and processes that leverage the latest AI tools to drive efficiencies across the purchasing team, including process optimization, analysis activities, and related operational areas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead talent development: hire, manage, develop, and mentor team members while driving critical projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute purchase orders and manage the escalation process for purchase-to-pay issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in engineering, supply chain, finance, or other discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in purchasing, supplier management, or contract negotiations; or a combination of these three areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a supervisory, lead, or management role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop spend strategy and execute on a specific plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud, compute, AI and data center contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with software and services categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience managing large value contracts/LTA’s with a global supply base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing a high volume of workload while setting and managing a strategy for your team’s commodities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge in current technologies and applications (e.g. MS Office Suite, AI tools, Atlassian, PowerBI, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective written, verbal, and presentation communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize appropriately to meet internal customer and company needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective written and verbal communications skills, with strong ability to communicate with all levels of internal personnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented, self-motivated, and able to respond quickly to a fast-moving and ever-changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conduct all activities with the highest of integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing forecasting and budgeting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work long hours and weekends if needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate outside of work hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to travel - up to 50% travel may be required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is based in Hawthorne, CA and requires being onsite - remote work not considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pay Range:&lt;br&gt;$175,000.00 - $245,000.00&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of your total rewards package at SpaceX. You may also be eligible for long-term incentives, in the form of company stock or long-term cash awards, as well as potential discretionary bonuses and the ability to purchase additional stock at a discount through an Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You will also receive access to comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, paid parental leave, and various other discounts and perks. You may also accrue 3 weeks of paid vacation and will be eligible for 10 or more paid holidays per year. Employees accrue paid sick leave pursuant to Company policy which satisfies or exceeds the accrual, carryover, and use requirements of the law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;SR. MANAGER, RETAIL CHANNEL MANAGEMENT (STARLINK CONSUMER)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;As the Sr. Manager of Retail Channel Management, known internally as Sr. Manager, Starlink Business Operations, you will lead global retail channel operations for the Starlink Consumer Business. You will sit in the central Consumer Growth support organization and bring the retail channel managers across every region into one operating team with shared processes, tools, and standards. You own how retail demand becomes product on the shelf: order intake and processing, inventory allocation, kit and accessory readiness, and launch support for new retail doors.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:220,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:220}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;You are the connective tissue between the regional growth teams that own retailer and distributor relationships and the Starlink functions that build, plan, and ship hardware (supply chain, demand planning, S&amp;amp;OP, logistics, production, compliance, and finance). In a fast-paced environment, you make sure retailer demand turns into accurate forecasts, the right kits and accessories arrive at distributor and retailer warehouses on time and retail ready, and issues are found and closed before they leave shelves empty.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:220,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:220}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:220,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:220}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Lead global retail channel operations for Starlink Consumer and set the operating standard for how retail and distribution partners are supported worldwide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Lead the global retail channel management team, including senior managers and retail operations leads, and consolidate retail channel team members across regions into one global team; define roles, coverage, and operating cadence; and direct the retail operations staff embedded in the regional growth organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Own the retail order lifecycle from purchase order to delivery: PO intake, order entry, allocation, fulfillment, shipment tracking, and receiving issues; standardize distributor and retailer order templates and drive automation wherever it removes manual work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Support new retail door openings and expansions, including launch checklists, initial load-in orders, inventory positioning, merchandising and fixture readiness, in-store activation setup, and handoffs to regional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Own retail inputs into demand planning and S&amp;amp;OP: consolidate distributor and retailer forecasts for kits and accessories by region, reconcile them against sell-in, sell-through, and inventory, and represent retail demand in production and supply planning reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Partner with supply chain, logistics, and regional distribution center (RDC) teams to balance retail and online inventory, prioritize retail orders, and keep weeks of supply, backorders, and aged orders inside plan&lt;/li&gt;
