&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SR. RF &amp;amp; WIRELESS COMPLIANCE ENGINEER (STARLINK)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is leveraging its experience building rockets and spacecraft to deploy Starlink, the world&#39;s most advanced broadband internet system. Starlink is the world&#39;s largest satellite constellation and provides fast, reliable internet to millions of users worldwide. We design, build, manufacture, and operate all parts of the system — including thousands of satellites and millions of customer kits. We are looking for best-in-class engineers to help maximize Starlink&#39;s utility for individuals, communities, and businesses.&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Starlink radio products must certify in the United States and internationally before they ship. This role is the RF compliance owner for those products, split&amp;nbsp;about 50/50 between:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own RF regulatory strategy and certification for Starlink wireless hardware on a 50/50&amp;nbsp;WiFi&amp;nbsp;and cellular mix across US and international markets&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WiFi&amp;nbsp;(2.4 / 5 / 6 GHz): develop and own compliance strategy, test setups, and methods for typical&amp;nbsp;WiFi&amp;nbsp;products, including DFS where required and 6 GHz / AFC paths as those products come online&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cellular (5G, LTE, GPRS, 3GPP): develop and own compliance strategy for cellular hardware, including base stations and related devices, covering US licensed-service rules and international 3GPP / ETSI requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply core FCC and ETSI radio standards in day-to-day work — including FCC Part 15 for&amp;nbsp;WiFi&amp;nbsp;(2.4 / 5 / 6 GHz, DFS) and FCC licensed-service rules for cellular; ETSI EN 300 328 (2.4 GHz), EN 301 893 (5 GHz), EN 303 687 (6 GHz WAS/RLAN), and EN 301 908 / 3GPP for cellular devices and base stations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read RF designs (architecture, radio chains, antennas, filters, power tables, firmware limits) and turn standards into actionable design and test requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and run RF compliance test campaigns with accredited labs — conducted and radiated, spurious, power, DFS, exposure (MPE/SAR) as applicable, and cellular / base-station conformance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with RF hardware, firmware, and software teams to implement the design or power-table changes required for certification&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate and generate transmit power tables with RF design, software, and test labs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit labs and vendors so methods and results are consistent and defensible&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and maintain technical files, test reports, and certification applications (FCC / ISED / RED and equivalent global filings)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support global market access when Starlink adds bands, power levels, or new&amp;nbsp;WiFi&amp;nbsp;/ cellular SKUs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide RF regulatory guidance to Product Compliance Engineers and RF design teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, or another STEM discipline&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in RF / wireless regulatory compliance and certification&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of basic FCC and ETSI radio standards for&amp;nbsp;WiFi&amp;nbsp;and/or cellular&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to follow an RF product from design → test → compliance (not test-only or paperwork-only)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on mix of&amp;nbsp;WiFi&amp;nbsp;(2.4, 5, and 6 GHz) and cellular (5G, LTE, GPRS/2G, 3GPP) —&amp;nbsp;including base stations — in both US and international certifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WiFi: FCC Part 15 (15.247 / 15.407), ETSI EN 300 328, EN 301 893, EN 303 687; DFS; 6 GHz / AFC&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cellular: 3GPP (LTE / NR and GPRS/GSM as applicable), ETSI EN 301 908 (devices and base stations), FCC Parts 22 / 24 / 27 (and related licensed-service rules); PTCRB / GCF for cellular hardware&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read RF schematics, block diagrams, antenna / layout choices, and firmware power limits, and to explain why a design will or will not pass&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining test setups and methodologies, not only witnessing lab tests&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running RF compliance campaigns and driving design changes to close failures&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record certifying high-volume wireless products (consumer, infrastructure, or both)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate standards into requirements RF and firmware teams can implement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours or weekends as needed for mission-critical certification deadlines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work on-site with RF design, test, and lab teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
