&lt;p&gt;As a Sr. Software Engineer on the Starlink Enterprise Products team you will define, build, and deploy product features and capabilities that unlock new opportunities to advance global connectivity. Your software will have a meaningful and measurable impact in areas such as aviation, maritime, transportation, healthcare, remote communities, research operations, media broadcast, datacenters, and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To succeed in this role, you must be a technically excellent first-principles problem solver. You must be a self-starter and have a passion for making things work in high-impact situations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop highly reliable real-time software&amp;nbsp;running&amp;nbsp;on network switches,&amp;nbsp;servers,&amp;nbsp;ground antennas,&amp;nbsp;and satellites&amp;nbsp;to optimize network performance&amp;nbsp;to support the most demanding applications and environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own&amp;nbsp;the impact of the&amp;nbsp;software&amp;nbsp;you create&amp;nbsp;over its complete lifecycle including&amp;nbsp;architecture design, implementation, testing, and support.&amp;nbsp;Incorporate&amp;nbsp;learnings&amp;nbsp;from real-world&amp;nbsp;deployments&amp;nbsp;to drive continual improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop tools&amp;nbsp;where needed to support testing, performance monitoring and troubleshooting of the systems that depend on your software.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build prototypes and manage experiments to prove out key design concepts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate next-generation networking technologies to direct data through an ever-changing network of satellites, ground stations, and users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
