&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;STARLINK CUSTOMER SUCCESS MANAGER (LATAM BACKHAUL)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Starlink is delivering high-speed, low-latency internet around the world. Customer Success is the post-sale owner of the customer relationship, where they are the single name on a book of enterprise accounts from contract signature through onboarding, activation, payment, and long-term growth. This role owns Starlink Backhaul / Layer 2 accounts in Latin America. You take assigned accounts from contract signature through onboarding, activation, payment, and expansion across the region. Sales books the deal. You own everything after.&amp;nbsp;This is an individual contributor role, and the ideal candidate is a self-starter who is comfortable operating without a defined playbook, holds a high bar of communication, and treats revenue, activation, and account health as their personal responsibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own assigned Latin America backhaul accounts from contract signature through onboarding, activation, day-to-day management, and long-term growth as the primary customer contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hit and exceed revenue targets on time by tracking readiness, shipments, activations, and payments, and by raising risks early when dates or dollars may slip&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep internal systems current so account status, risk, and opportunity are visible in one place&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor account health—including contract compliance, KPI performance, invoicing and tax, logistics, and the customer relationship—to prevent delayed cash or churn&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear expectations with customers and partners on what SpaceX can and cannot commit to on timing and delivery&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build account plans that define current state, a healthy account, and the next dollar of revenue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify expansion, additional sites or kits, and new ways customers can use Starlink backhaul&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate leadership business reviews that connect Starlink performance to customer results&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast retention and revenue for the book so leadership can plan against a real number&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring customer feedback into SpaceX and work with engineering, support, finance, and operations to reduce errors across accounts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape how we operate backhaul in Latin America, including country-level priorities, onboarding, local billing and tax, and getting paid&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document processes that support expansion and scaling of the business&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering, business, or a related field, OR high school diploma / equivalency certificate and 6+ years of professional experience in account management, customer success, business development, operations, or a technical customer-facing role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years owning a defined book of business with accountability for customer health and revenue (retention, realization, expansion, or collections), not just project delivery&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years supporting customers on a technical product or service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in Spanish and/or Portuguese (written and spoken)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
