&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;STARLINK PRODUCT GROWTH DIRECTOR (PRICING &amp;amp; MONETIZATION STRATEGY)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Starlink consumer growth depends on a clear monetization strategy: the right plans and prices, a sharp value proposition, and an honest read of whether we are on goal. This role owns three things: plan and pricing strategy, growth team reporting, and the growth metrics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own plan and pricing strategy: how we structure product pricing and service plan pricing, the in-market value proposition, and willingness to pay. You will work with global go-to-market teams on performance goal setting and tracking, and you will model impact with financial planning and accounting before decisions go to market and after they are live.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the growth metrics and the growth team’s reporting against them: how the overall growth team is doing toward goal, where the gaps are, and who needs to fix them, where, and by when. You will understand what each market needs, when it needs it, and what it will take to close the gap. You support the business operations of in-market GTM teams and serve as the central orchestrator between those teams and Growth Central, so in-market teams have what they need to be successful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend and validate product pricing and service plan pricing structures; build the pre-launch impact model and the post-launch readout with financial planning and accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global go-to-market teams on value propositions, willingness to pay, and performance goal setting and tracking by market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the growth metrics and the growth scoreboard: report how the overall growth team is tracking to goal, name the gaps, and specify who owns the fix, in which market, and by when&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clear view of in-market needs (offer, price, capacity, program, tooling) and what it will take to close each gap; keep Growth Central and GTM on one set of numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the business operations of go-to-market teams in market: what they need from Growth Central, when they need it, and whether it actually landed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as connective tissue between in-market GTM and Growth Central so commercial decisions, forecasts, and asks do not get lost between teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the pricing and performance toolkit (models, trackers, decision memos) so recommendations can be reviewed, challenged, and shipped&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in business, finance, economics, engineering, or STEM discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in pricing, monetization, financial planning, strategy, growth analytics, or a related commercial role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in pricing, monetization, FP&amp;amp;A, or commercial strategy for subscription, telecommunications, broadband, or consumer hardware-plus-service businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience setting or changing list price, plan architecture, or packaging, and living with the in-market result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modeling and comfort partnering with FP&amp;amp;A and accounting on forecast, actuals, and margin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting performance goals with in-country GTM teams and running a recurring impact cadence (weekly/monthly scoreboard, gap-to-goal, owners)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in willingness-to-pay, competitive price architecture, and market-specific value propositions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel required; SQL or BI tools strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating as a senior IC who can also stand up a small team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting distributed go-to-market teams from a central growth or commercial function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership presence in a fast-paced, high-scrutiny environment: clear recommendations, named tradeoffs, no buried assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as needed to support global go-to-market teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work extended hours and weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;STARLINK PRODUCTION ASSOCIATE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the most ambitious missions that SpaceX has undertaken to date, the Starlink satellite constellation is our solution to providing fast and reliable internet to the entire world. This facility in Bastrop, TX manufactures the high-volume consumer products that we ship directly to customers. Our customers currently include teachers in the most remote parts of the Amazon, researchers in Antarctica, digital nomads who travel via RV, emergency responders, commercial airlines, cruise lines, and residential users who live in more rural or developing areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Production Associate position supports the Starlink product factory and manufacturing operation, which continues to grow as demand for Starlink increases globally. This is a hands-on position that operates light equipment and performs basic assembly tasks in an organized and efficient manner. We are looking for motivated and well-rounded workers to help ensure the productivity and reliability of our manufacturing facility, ultimately ensuring that we can produce thousands of Starlink kits every day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of prototype manufacturing and test capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical/electrical assembly of user terminal components, subassemblies, and final assembly according to instructions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate light equipment such as drills, custom build tooling, crimpers, and presses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program, load, operate, and troubleshoot automated equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute equipment maintenance and calibration schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain consumables inventory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist engineers with development builds and other tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop and optimize production line stations and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a clean, organized, and thoroughly maintained workspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure product quality and conformance to design requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put safety as number one priority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of mechanical or electrical assembly experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to read, interpret, and work from drawings and controlled documentation such as: layout drawings, mechanical drawings, assembly procedures/work instructions, schematics, engineering drawings, and parts lists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to proficiently use a PC, Microsoft Windows, and Microsoft Office suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an electro-mechanical manufacturing company, a precision manufacturing company, or high-volume manufacturing company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with electrical wiring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electro-mechanical assembly and prototype development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting up and running tests and experiments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available to work at least one of the following shifts:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Shift: 5 AM - 5:30 PM (Sunday through Tuesday and every other Wednesday)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B Shift: 5 AM - 5:30 PM (Thursday through Saturday and every other Wednesday)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C Shift: 5 PM - 5:30 AM (Sunday through Tuesday and every other Wednesday)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;D Shift: 5 PM - 5:30 AM (Thursday through Saturday and every other Wednesday)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work all shifts, overtime and weekends as needed. Shifts are subject to change, we have multiple shifts, including late afternoons/nights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standing for long periods of time, climbing up and down ladders, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, and stretching may be required to perform the functions of this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to lift up to 25lbs. unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
