&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUPPLY CHAIN RELIABILITY ENGINEER (FALCON)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Supply Chain team is responsible for the sourcing, planning, procurement, warehousing, and transportation of all raw materials and components needed to build our revolutionary spacecraft and launch vehicles. Our mission is to get the right part in the right place at the right time, every time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX demands a new type of supply chain. We require our suppliers to provide premium quality with rapidly evolving designs at increasingly ambitious volumes. We are actively looking for candidates who possess comprehensive knowledge of manufacturing and quality tools and have unrelenting motivation to enable supply chain for success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;To be successful, you will need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A practical knowledge of manufacturing processes and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to lead projects, help develop strategy, drive cross-functional team accountability, and deliver results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for continuous improvement and a patience to shepherd ideas from initial requirements through execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to roll up your sleeves and step into unknown situations to understand the current state and most optimal path forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to be a voice of reason for reliability and ensure that product reliability risks are considered within Supply Chain processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to build relationships with cross-functional groups to identify, prioritize, and close any reliability or process gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to lead groups in creating and refining ideas or solutions to problems, communicating the benefits of change, and keeping related projects on track&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and own reliability-focused improvement projects to help the Supply Chain team meet its reliability goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and analyze trends in Supply Chain Reliability data and drive improvements in supplier performance, drive reduction in non-conformances on purchased parts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with Supply Chain, Production operations, Inspection, Shipping/Receiving, and Engineering teams to develop appropriate quality signals and processes to meet overall program reliability goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain established quality processes and necessary procedures to ensure the identification, segregation, control, and disposition of all nonconforming materials, parts, components, and subassemblies at the business and supplier level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for risk reduction and removal of complexity in designs and processes to improve quality performance, collaborate with integrated product teams to drive improvements and address high-impact and recurring non-conformances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
