&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in an engineering field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in quality systems, quality assurance/control, and/or manufacturing/production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of AS9100, ISO 9000 and/or Nadcap AC7004&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in engineering or supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate autonomously with good written, oral, and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL, software development &amp;amp; project management, process flow mapping, material planning systems, warehouse management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to think big, align teams and organizations behind a goal, and execute with sustained results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of quality tools such as Lean principles, Six Sigma, root cause analysis and corrective action, advanced product quality planning (APQP), metrology, process failure mode and effects analysis (PFMEA), control plans, and various problem-solving approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high volume manufacturing (i.e. small or large machined components, hardware, COTS, fittings, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of supplier quality processes (production part approval process, advanced product quality planning, first article inspection reports, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disciplined approach to problem solving - 8D&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

