&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience with electrical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering or education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years as a heavy equipment and extended reach vehicle operator/trainer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master electrician license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with ERP software, Microsoft Office, video editing, and online training module development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently analyze, review, and research electrical and manufacturing processes and applicable codes, rules, regulations, and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of electrical install, maintenance, and troubleshooting (fixture/component repair, circuit testing, preventative maintenance, machinery electrical/electronic systems, hydraulic and pneumatic devices)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to test, calibrate, diagnose, and repair devices; use electrician’s hand tools and measuring/testing instruments, including precision instruments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings, blueprints, wiring diagrams, schematics, technical manuals, and reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written training and communication skills; proficiency developing training programs, materials, and student assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-oriented self-starter able to meet/exceed objectives in a multi-project environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
